`,r.jsxs(e.p,{children:["The left hand side names the artefact or technique (",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"ssh_key"}),", ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"cron_hijack"}),", ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"sudo_binary"}),", ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"pspy"}),", ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"file_upload"}),", ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"kerberoast"}),", ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"mssql_link"}),"), the right hand side is the destination node. The Graph plugin treats it as a normal link, so it shows up as an edge, but Dataview can also query these fields later if you want to generate a table of every pivot in the vault."]}),`
