`,r.jsx(e.p,{children:"The setting that actually changes how I work in practice is the Local Graph pane, pinned to the right hand sidebar. It shows only the neighbours of the note you are currently looking at, up to a configurable depth."}),`
`,r.jsxs(e.p,{children:["When I am sitting on ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"alice@10.10.10.30"})," writing up the privesc steps, the local graph already shows me the places this identity can reach. If one of those nodes is not yet ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"#pwned"}),", the colour difference tells me where there is still work to do without leaving the note."]}),`
