`,r.jsxs(e.p,{children:["At first, ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"switch"})," is a symbolic link to ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"/usr/bin"}),". The submitted string does not match ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"^/usr/bin/true$"}),", but canonicalising its parent produces ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"/usr/bin/true"}),", which does match."]}),`
`,r.jsxs(e.p,{children:["In sudo 1.9.17p2, ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"command_matches_regex()"})," uses that canonical path to perform the match and command checks. After a successful fallback match, however, it does not set ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"ctx->runas.cmnd"})," to the path that was actually checked. The frontend can therefore retain the original user-controlled pathname for the eventual ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"exec"}),"."]}),`
