`,r.jsxs(e.p,{children:["Settings that cause sudo to execute a securely retained descriptor may prevent this particular pathname swap. ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"fdexec=always"})," does this for path-matched commands. Under the default ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"fdexec=digest_only"})," setting, adding a command digest also causes sudo to execute the retained descriptor. A digest is not sufficient by itself when an administrator has explicitly configured ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"fdexec=never"}),". Filesystem policy such as ",r.jsx(e.code,{children:"noexec"}),", SELinux, or AppArmor can also change exploitability. Those are environmental mitigations, not a correction of the identity mismatch."]}),`
